      "updated": 1769103214421,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Scheduler Service",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "BNHMbsKsts5_VTLHAFWSJ",
      "originalText": "Scheduler Service",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-qyaB2b7utTDsE9CZoFd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5910.339486628932,
      "y": 4405.749585083963,
      "width": 740.3208751211487,
      "height": 980,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1286034359,
      "version": 2845,
      "versionNonce": 155136112,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769103214421,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Scheduler Service:\n- This will manage delays.\n- In redis I'll create minute wise time buckets, if delay is less that a minute I'll keep it at the\nservice layer itself(I'll spawn a goroutine which delays and executes the next action).\n- This scheduler service will run a cron job every minute and check in redis what are the Jobs\npending in it's current minute bucket and push it to a queue to execute the next action.\n- Once the action is completed I'll mark it's status as COMPLETED from SCHEDULED\n- This service can also be horizontally scaled quite extensively where I can assign each\ninstance with a node ID and each instance will have it's own time bucket in redis suffixed with\nit's node ID \n\n[2026::01::20::01::55::::NODE1]= [JobIds]\n[2026::01::20::01::55::::NODE1_TEMP]= [JobIds]\n\nI will keep 2 redis keys, one where it is getting scheduled and the other a temp key.\n\n[CODE BLOCk START]\n    Pop all currently scheduled jobIds from redis\n    Push all currently scheduled jobIds to temp\n    // above 2 statements will be atomic using LUA Script\n    For loop [JobIds]\n        Mark the Job as RUNNING\n        Push to destinationQ with the job details\n        Mark the Job as COMPLETED\n        Pop the job from TEMP key\n[CODE BLOCk END]\n\nThere will be a separate cron running every minute and keep checking the temp key of 5\nminutes before to see if there are any keys that had been missed.\n\nThis service will also expose a POST API to schedule the messages\n/ POST [Schedule Message]\n    - will send job details and the destination queue where data has to be pushed after a\ncertain delay\n\nJOB_SCHEDULER MODEL:\n{\n    jobID: \"some-unique-ID\" // Partition Key\n    executedAt: unixMilli\n    createdAt: unixMilli\n    updatedAt: unixMilli,\n    jobName: \"some name not needed unique\"\n    jobDetails: {\n        // will contain meta info of which signal triggered it and some other info\n    }\n    qName: \"name-of-queue\" // Name of the queue where it will be pushed with the job details\n    status: SCHEDULED | RUNNING | COMPLETED\n}\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Scheduler Service:\n- This will manage delays.\n- In redis I'll create minute wise time buckets, if delay is less that a minute I'll keep it at the service layer itself(I'll spawn a goroutine which delays and executes the next action).\n- This scheduler service will run a cron job every minute and check in redis what are the Jobs pending in it's current minute bucket and push it to a queue to execute the next action.\n- Once the action is completed I'll mark it's status as COMPLETED from SCHEDULED\n- This service can also be horizontally scaled quite extensively where I can assign each instance with a node ID and each instance will have it's own time bucket in redis suffixed with it's node ID \n\n[2026::01::20::01::55::::NODE1]= [JobIds]\n[2026::01::20::01::55::::NODE1_TEMP]= [JobIds]\n\nI will keep 2 redis keys, one where it is getting scheduled and the other a temp key.\n\n[CODE BLOCk START]\n    Pop all currently scheduled jobIds from redis\n    Push all currently scheduled jobIds to temp\n    // above 2 statements will be atomic using LUA Script\n    For loop [JobIds]\n        Mark the Job as RUNNING\n        Push to destinationQ with the job details\n        Mark the Job as COMPLETED\n        Pop the job from TEMP key\n[CODE BLOCk END]\n\nThere will be a separate cron running every minute and keep checking the temp key of 5 minutes before to see if there are any keys that had been missed.\n\nThis service will also expose a POST API to schedule the messages\n/ POST [Schedule Message]\n    - will send job details and the destination queue where data has to be pushed after a certain delay\n\nJOB_SCHEDULER MODEL:\n{\n    jobID: \"some-unique-ID\" // Partition Key\n    executedAt: unixMilli\n    createdAt: unixMilli\n    updatedAt: unixMilli,\n    jobName: \"some name not needed unique\"\n    jobDetails: {\n        // will contain meta info of which signal triggered it and some other info\n    }\n    qName: \"name-of-queue\" // Name of the queue where it will be pushed with the job details\n    status: SCHEDULED | RUNNING | COMPLETED\n}\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
