    },
    {
      "id": "kfpM4s_ryQdOfzU8RLHAF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4915.891446081433,
      "y": 3280.919171296544,
      "width": 805.5736391155012,
      "height": 1420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 274469751,
      "version": 7374,
      "versionNonce": 1598932592,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769103214421,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Ingestion Service:\nThis service consists of two essential parts one is my Workflow Manager which manages all the\nworkflows and the other is a Workflow Executor which executes a workflow on receiving a signal.\n\nWorkflow Manager:\n- On startup of service it will fetch all the workflows from the database or I can keep the workflows\nhardcoded in the codebase for now, if I keep it in db the model will contain only the workflow IDs.\nWORKFLOWS MODEL:\n{\n    \"workflowID\": \"some-unique-ID\" // PK\n}\nIt will fetch all the workflows\nCheck in Zookeeper what the current workflow version is.\nLoad it in memory, I will only keep the latest one in memory.\nIf any workflow is currently running in an older version and is not in memory I'll fetch is lazily taking a\nlock and load it in memory.\nThe entire purpose of this manager will be to keep them in memory.\n\nAPIs Exposed by the library:\n    /POST workflow\n        - Add new workflow details in DB (WORKFLOW MODEL)\n        - Add new ZNode\n        - In the existing ZNode named ZKRefreshNode store the new updatedAt\n\n        ZKRefreshNode watcher:\n        If the value changes add all the new workflows based on workflowID and version will not\ndiscard the older versions.\n        All the services get updated with the new node.\n    \n    /GET workflows:\n        - Return all the workflows that are present in the database with pagination\n\nWorkflow Executor:\n- This service will injest multiple signals at scale and execute the workflow attached to it\n- Whenever it receives a signal it will push to an ExecutorQ and store the data.\n\nAPIs Exposed:\n    /POST signal\n        - Push to ExecutorQ\n        - Store in DynamoDB the signal information with dedup check\n\n\n    /GET runs\n        - Based on the GSI(status_created_at) return paginated info of the recently running\nworkflows based on their statuses.\n        \n    /GET runs: id\n        - Return details of the workflow that being executed by the signal.\n\n    \nExecutorQ:\nFetch from the Signal Model which signal to work upon.\nCheck the workflow manager if the workflowId and version exists.\nIf not the workflow manager will fetch it and store it in memory.\nIf evaluations are not performed:\n    Check the evaluations that needs to be performed.\n        For loop Evaluations:\n            If Evaluations are successful move them to the new state based on the evaluationIndex\n        end\nIf evaluations are performed:\n    Check the actions that needs to be performed.\n        For loop Actions:\n            Do the necessary action\n            If it includes delay POST /schedule with jobDetails being the same Qbody as the\nExecutorQ.\n            Update status of action executed\n        end\n    Acknowledge message.\n\nOnce delay is complete scheduler will push it to the same Q where it will check all the conditions and\nperform the remaining actions.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ingestion Service:\nThis service consists of two essential parts one is my Workflow Manager which manages all the workflows and the other is a Workflow Executor which executes a workflow on receiving a signal.\n\nWorkflow Manager:\n- On startup of service it will fetch all the workflows from the database or I can keep the workflows hardcoded in the codebase for now, if I keep it in db the model will contain only the workflow IDs.\nWORKFLOWS MODEL:\n{\n    \"workflowID\": \"some-unique-ID\" // PK\n}\nIt will fetch all the workflows\nCheck in Zookeeper what the current workflow version is.\nLoad it in memory, I will only keep the latest one in memory.\nIf any workflow is currently running in an older version and is not in memory I'll fetch is lazily taking a lock and load it in memory.\nThe entire purpose of this manager will be to keep them in memory.\n\nAPIs Exposed by the library:\n    /POST workflow\n        - Add new workflow details in DB (WORKFLOW MODEL)\n        - Add new ZNode\n        - In the existing ZNode named ZKRefreshNode store the new updatedAt\n\n        ZKRefreshNode watcher:\n        If the value changes add all the new workflows based on workflowID and version will not discard the older versions.\n        All the services get updated with the new node.\n    \n    /GET workflows:\n        - Return all the workflows that are present in the database with pagination\n\nWorkflow Executor:\n- This service will injest multiple signals at scale and execute the workflow attached to it\n- Whenever it receives a signal it will push to an ExecutorQ and store the data.\n\nAPIs Exposed:\n    /POST signal\n        - Push to ExecutorQ\n        - Store in DynamoDB the signal information with dedup check\n\n\n    /GET runs\n        - Based on the GSI(status_created_at) return paginated info of the recently running workflows based on their statuses.\n        \n    /GET runs: id\n        - Return details of the workflow that being executed by the signal.\n\n    \nExecutorQ:\nFetch from the Signal Model which signal to work upon.\nCheck the workflow manager if the workflowId and version exists.\nIf not the workflow manager will fetch it and store it in memory.\nIf evaluations are not performed:\n    Check the evaluations that needs to be performed.\n        For loop Evaluations:\n            If Evaluations are successful move them to the new state based on the evaluationIndex\n        end\nIf evaluations are performed:\n    Check the actions that needs to be performed.\n        For loop Actions:\n            Do the necessary action\n            If it includes delay POST /schedule with jobDetails being the same Qbody as the ExecutorQ.\n            Update status of action executed\n        end\n    Acknowledge message.\n\nOnce delay is complete scheduler will push it to the same Q where it will check all the conditions and perform the remaining actions.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
